  "handoff": "# Canonical session handoff\n\nCreated at: 2026-08-06T22:55:40.975Z\nUpdated at: 2026-08-06T23:13:27Z\nReason: Preserve the canonical resume context after completing the Toast/ToastStack foundation work, recording the deferred theme/effect audit, and returning planner focus to the current in-progress app context-menu phase.\n\n## Current focus\n\n- Feature: `F006` — 🛠️ App / Chrome Features — **in-progress**\n- Phase: `P031(F006)` — app-11: Right-click context menu — **in-progress**\n- Task: `P031(F006)/T144` — Terminal pane right-click context menu — **planned**\n\nNo task is currently in progress in P031. T144 is the sole remaining planned task and is the validated resume candidate; T153 (ContextMenu grid-ui widget) and T158 (sidebar right-click context menu) are done.\n\n## What was being done\n\nThe session completed `P058(F009)` — Toast / ToastStack Widget Foundation, including the previously failed GPU UAT around exit fragments, smooth vertical reflow, viewport overflow behavior, and pass-through.\n`Toast` now uses real retained children; `ToastStack` reconciles same-ID payload changes, preserves transition/runtime state, supports inert exit animations, reports real hint targets, and damages both previous and current motion bounds.\nThe showcase demonstrates batch insertion, same-ID update, action, dismiss, non-dismissible cards, enter/exit/reflow, and page-layer pass-through.\nThe final T394 test pass added explicit move/press/release miss routing, exactly-once action/dismiss behavior, and tick/repaint/damage coverage.\n`cargo test -p heca-grid-ui toast_` passed 20 relevant tests and `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features` passed; only the pre-existing upstream `block v0.1.6` future-incompatibility warning remains.\nA separate audit found local glow/bracket/ToastStack effect metrics and a MarkerGroup double-strength scaling issue. The user explicitly deferred that work; it is recorded under `F010/P094/T396` and must not be folded into the context-menu task.\nNo commit, push, branch mutation, or PR operation was performed.\n\n## How to resume\n\n1. Run `handoff_show` for `P031(F006)` and `task_get(full=true)` for `T144` to confirm the planner still identifies Terminal pane right-click context menu as the next task.\n2. Inspect the existing reusable implementation and completed sidebar integration first: `heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/context_menu.rs`, `heca/src/chrome/context_menu.rs`, `heca/src/mouse/interactive.rs`, `heca/src/mouse/hit_test.rs`, `heca/src/mouse/target.rs`, and `heca/src/app/interaction.rs`.\n3. Perform the mandatory written pre-flight: name the existing `ContextMenu` widget and existing action/interaction path; do not build inline app UI or bypass ActionRegistry/KeymapRegistry/RPC reachability.\n4. Before any code edit, call `task_start` for `P031(F006)/T144`.\n5. Run a baseline `cargo check`, implement the terminal-pane right-click path as a small behavior-preserving slice, and add focused mouse/interaction tests.\n6. Validate with targeted tests, `cargo check`, and `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features`; run GPU/manual verification for the terminal menu before completing T144.\n7. Keep all changes uncommitted unless the user explicitly authorizes each git mutation.\n\n## Files touched\n\nSource/documentation files modified by the Toast/ToastStack work in this session:\n\n- `heca-grid-ui/src/component.rs`\n- `heca-grid-ui/src/hint.rs`\n- `heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/toast.rs`\n- `heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/toast_stack.rs`\n- `heca-grid-ui/tests/phase_a.rs`\n- `heca-renderer/examples/showcase.rs`\n- `heca-view-realize/src/lib.rs`\n- `docs/widgets.md`\n\nPlanner entities modified/created during this session:\n\n- `.planner/phases/949d48a4-6001-42b2-a12c-25ba69a95c24.json` — P058 completion and task state\n- `.planner/phases/cd9bbc0d-5e78-4656-8f5f-c7c6ee089220.json` — new P094 effect-token normalization phase and T396\n- `.planner/generated/PLAN.md` and generated feature/phase views regenerated by `plan_render`\n\nThe worktree already contains broad pre-existing planner/generated changes; do not assume every dirty planner file was authored by this session and do not reset or commit them without explicit user direction.\n\n## Blockers\n\nNone recorded.\n\n## Next steps\n\n1. Start and implement `P031(F006)/T144` — Terminal pane right-click context menu.\n2. Reuse the completed generic `ContextMenu` widget and sidebar integration patterns; add terminal-specific app bindings only above grid-ui.\n3. After T144 passes automated and manual verification, complete it so P031 can derive to done.\n4. Leave `F010/P094/T396` deferred until the user explicitly chooses to schedule the effect-token normalization.\n\n## Recent decisions\n\n- The glow/bracket/ToastStack metric inconsistency is real but will **not** be fixed now; it was filed as `F010/P094/T396`.\n- The ToastStack showcase capacity (`max_visible`) remains host-owned lifecycle policy, not a Theme/widget token.\n- The corrected ToastStack exit/reflow behavior was accepted through GPU UAT, and P058 was completed.\n- No automatic commit or other git mutation is permitted; wait for explicit user authorization.\n\n## Reminder\n\nWhen work on P031 has been fully resumed and the handoff context has been absorbed, clear this phase handoff explicitly with `handoff_clear` for `P031(F006)`.",
